# WebSocket Server URL
# 
# By default, the client will automatically connect to:
# - wss://irgri.uk/ws (when served over HTTPS - production)
# - ws://localhost:3001/ws (when served over HTTP - local development)
#
# You can override this behavior by setting VITE_WS_URL:

# For custom server (uncomment and modify):
# VITE_WS_URL=wss://your-custom-domain.com/ws

# For local development with custom port:
# VITE_WS_URL=ws://localhost:3001/ws

# For production Netlify deployment:
# Set this in Netlify environment variables:
# VITE_WS_URL=wss://irgri.uk/ws
